  "artifact_text": "### Observations\n\n1. Pod `notifications-worker-6784d8b8df-lk5l8` is in `CrashLoopBackOff` with exit code 1 (`Error`) and 13 restarts (pod status).\n2. Pod logs show: `ERROR notifications-worker: missing required setting SMTP_PASSWORD (environment variable is unset or empty)` followed by exit 1.\n3. Deployment `notifications-worker` mounts `SMTP_PASSWORD` via an optional `secretKeyRef` to Secret `notifications-smtp` (deployment spec `notifications-worker`), rolled out in deployment change `CI-2459`.\n\n### Ruled-out Leads\n\n1. Pod memory exhaustion or OOMKills like INC-2025-0207 were ruled out because the container terminated with exit code 1, not 137 (`OOMKilled`).\n2. An unhandled application code exception was ruled out because the startup validation intentionally exited due to missing required environment variables.\n\n### Root Cause\n\nDeployment `notifications-worker` v2.0.0 (`CI-2459`) requires `SMTP_PASSWORD`, but the referenced Secret `notifications-smtp` lacks the `SMTP_PASSWORD` key, causing startup validation failure.\n\n### Recommended Action\n\nThe notifications team must add the key `SMTP_PASSWORD` to Secret `notifications-smtp` or update the deployment manifest's `secretKeyRef` to reference the correct Secret key.",
